    "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to determine the length of one of its sides. We are given two expressions for the length of the side: \\(4x - 15\\) meters and \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\).\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nFirst, we will isolate \\(x\\) by adding \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\nNext, we add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\nNow, we solve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides by 7:\n\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nWith \\(x\\) found, we substitute \\(x = 5\\) back into one of the original expressions to find the length of the side of the square. We can use either expression, but let's use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of one side of the square is 5 meters. The area of a square is given by the square of the length of one of its sides. Therefore, the area is:\n\n\\[\n5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
